LOCATION:LOWELL E. BAIER HALL/IU MAURER SCHOOL OF LAW
GEO:39.165074;-86.526424
SUMMARY:Indiana Tax Court Oral Argument
DESCRIPTION:The Indiana Tax Court will visit the IU Maurer School of Law 
 to hear oral argument in Northern Indiana Public Service Company\, LLC v.
  Indiana Department of State Revenue\, Case No. 24T-TA-00017.   The Tax C
 ourt is a specialized appellate court with exclusive jurisdiction over ap
 peals from final determinations of the Indiana Department of State Revenu
 e and the Indiana Board of Tax Review and certain appeals from the Depart
 ment of Local Government Finance. It hears disputes over state and local 
 taxes\, including property\, income\, sales\, and excise taxes\, which to
 uch the finances of Hoosier individuals\, families\, and businesses alike
 .  Attendees will have a rare chance to see this specialized court in act
 ion. Because the Tax Court's decisions are reviewed directly by the India
 na Supreme Court\, rather than by the Court of Appeals\, the proceedings 
 offer a distinctive look at how Indiana's tax system is shaped by the jud
 iciary.  A summary of the case can be found here (https://events.iu.edu/l
 ive/files/8523-nipsco-bench-memopdf). Following the argument\, attendees 
 may participate in an informal Q&amp\;A session with the judge and attorn
 eys. While food is not permitted during the argument\, food is allowed du
 ring the Q&amp\;A.  Attendees are asked to observe courtroom etiquette:Re
 move hats before entering the courtroom.  Stand when judges enter and lea
 ve the courtroom.  Turn off or silence cell phones before entering the co
 urtroom. Do not use phones while court is in session.  No video\, audio r
 ecording\, or photography is allowed once court is in session.  No food o
 r beverages are allowed in the courtroom  Refrain from speaking during th
 e proceedings
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The Indiana Tax Court will visit the IU
  Maurer School of Law to hear oral argument in <em>Northern Indiana Publi
 c Service Company\, LLC v. Indiana Department of State Revenue</em>\, Cas
 e No. 24T-TA-00017. <em></em></p><p>  The Tax Court is a specialized appe
 llate court with exclusive jurisdiction over appeals from final determina
 tions of the Indiana Department of State Revenue and the Indiana Board of
  Tax Review and certain appeals from the Department of Local Government F
 inance. It hears disputes over state and local taxes\, including property
 \, income\, sales\, and excise taxes\, which touch the finances of Hoosie
 r individuals\, families\, and businesses alike.</p><p>  Attendees will h
 ave a rare chance to see this specialized court in action. Because the Ta
 x Court's decisions are reviewed directly by the Indiana Supreme Court\, 
 rather than by the Court of Appeals\, the proceedings offer a distinctive
  look at how Indiana's tax system is shaped by the judiciary.</p><p>  A <
 a class="file file_8523 lw_files_pdf" title="NIPSCO _ Bench Memo.pdf" hre
 f="https://events.iu.edu/live/files/8523-nipsco-bench-memopdf" target="_b
 lank" rel="noopener">summary of the case can be found here</a>. Following
  the argument\, attendees may participate in an informal Q&amp\;A session
  with the judge and attorneys. While food is not permitted during the arg
 ument\, food is allowed during the Q&amp\;A.</p><p>  Attendees are asked 
 to observe courtroom etiquette:</p><ul><li>Remove hats before entering th
 e courtroom.  </li><li>Stand when judges enter and leave the courtroom.  
 </li><li>Turn off or silence cell phones before entering the courtroom. D
 o not use phones while court is in session.  </li><li>No video\, audio re
 cording\, or photography is allowed once court is in session.  </li><li>N
 o food or beverages are allowed in the courtroom  </li><li>Refrain from s
 peaking during the proceedings  </li></ul>
UID:20261119T170000Z-2377394@events.iu.edu
